  "why_0_134_became_1_428": "The 0.134 SOL figure counted only network fees plus a narrow verified-tip set (Jito, and sometimes a handful of swap-adjacent transfers already treated as tips). Item 8 then enumerated every native SOL withdrawal. Vanity recipients resembling Astralane / Nozomi / Node1 / NextBlock plus wyvPk\u2026 and soyastP\u2026 were previously bundled into 'fees+tips' or ignored. At aa2ef2d those non-Jito withdrawals were moved to unverified outside debits, producing 1.428081532 SOL. Under that sensitivity +0.242261753 \u2212 1.428081532 \u2248 \u22121.186 SOL, so the sign flips.",
  "why_figures_changed_again_after_published_lists": "This pass pins published tip-account lists (coverage/PUBLISHED_TIP_ACCOUNTS.json). Recipients that match Nozomi, Astralane, NextBlock or Node1 published accounts are verified tips and are deducted from net. Recipients that only resemble those names (wyvPkWjVZz1M8fHQnMMCDTQDbkManefNNhweYk5WkcF, soyastP66xyYC8XADXZjdMM5BAVGD2YRvz8dwtLsqb8) stay unverified. Failed-transaction transfers are excluded (only meta.fee executed). Executed full-wallet unresolved is 0.296680516 SOL, equal to swap-adjacent sensitivity; executed full-wallet verified tips are 1.131401016 SOL; scoped net is 0.120294936 SOL. 0.120 \u2212 0.297 < 0, so CccS still cannot be a provisional_research_lead.",
  "failed_transactions_excluded": "Failed transactions contribute only meta.fee. Transfers in those transactions did not execute and are omitted from verified tips and unresolved debits.",
